#: includes/help.php
msgid "The Simple Kit PDF Plugin"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "This plugin embeds PDF files in posts and pages using pdf.js, the open source PDF viewer maintained by Mozilla. The document is rendered directly in the visitor browser, so no external service is contacted and the file is never uploaded anywhere else."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Highlights"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "PDF files from the Media Library or from any URL hosted on this site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Optional toolbar with page navigation, zoom and fit-to-width controls."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Optional download button, controlled per block."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "The library only loads on pages that actually contain a PDF block, and only when the block approaches the viewport."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "How the plugin works"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Edit a post or page and add the block \"Simple Kit PDF\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Choose a PDF from the Media Library, or switch the source to \"Manual URL\" and type a URL for a PDF hosted on this site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Adjust the block settings in the sidebar and publish."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "On the frontend the PDF is displayed with pdf.js, occupying the full width of the block."
msgstr ""

