msgid "Full document"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Fixed height keeps the block at the chosen pixel height. First page fits exactly one page. Full document fits every page of the document, including the spacing between them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
#: assets/block.js
msgid "Fixed height (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Used by the fixed height mode, between 100 and 2000 pixels. The width always follows the block width."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "The first page and full document modes are measured in the browser after the PDF is loaded, so they follow the current zoom level. The fixed height value is used only while the document is loading, and a long document can make the block very tall."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
#: assets/block.js
msgid "Show toolbar"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Disabled"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Shows the controls above the document: previous/next page, page number, zoom, fit width and, optionally, download."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
#: assets/block.js
msgid "Allow download"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Only available when the toolbar is visible. Adds a download button to the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Same domain requirement"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Only PDF files hosted on this site can be embedded. URLs pointing to other domains are refused both by the block editor and by the renderer, which prevents the block from being used to frame third-party content."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "About the download control"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Disabling the download button removes the control and the no-JavaScript fallback link, but it is a display policy, not an access restriction. Any visitor can still read the file URL from the page source, exactly as with an image displayed on the page. If the document must be protected, use a membership or protected-files plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "The block keeps showing \"Loading PDF...\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "The viewer is loaded as a JavaScript module and uses a module worker. Some security plugins and strict Content-Security-Policy rules block module workers. Check the browser console for errors and allow the plugin files (assets/pdfjs/build/pdf.worker.mjs) to be loaded as a script."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Some characters are missing or replaced in a PDF."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "The plugin ships a reduced pdf.js build without the optional CJK character maps (cmaps) and standard font fallbacks. PDFs that depend on those make the browser substitute glyphs. Embedding the fonts in the PDF avoids the problem."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "Very large files feel slow."
msgstr ""

#: includes/help.php
msgid "pdf.js downloads the file in the browser. Prefer optimized PDFs (for example, with compressed images) and avoid files with hundreds of pages on landing pages."
msgstr ""

